# Branch (c): the `E₁` obstruction `Ω` is an exact square over `K₅`

`Ω(t₂, s₂) = c₁ s₂² + c₂ t₂² s₂ + c₃ t₂⁴` is the `E₁` compatibility condition
(`branch_c/scripts/branch_c_stage6e_patch101.py`: `Omega`, the left null vector of the 19×19 `E₁`
operator dotted with `RHS_{E₁}`). Its three coefficients lie in `K₅ = ℚ[w]/(w⁵ − w⁴ + 3w³ + 3w² + 26)`.
They are written here exactly as polynomials in `w` (extracted by `gen_omega_lean.py` from the corrected
pipeline run; the three values coincide in the original and corrected runs).

Proved over every field `L` of characteristic `0` and every root `w ∈ L` of `R`:

* `omega_disc_zero` — `c₂² − 4 c₁ c₃ = 0`: the discriminant vanishes in characteristic `0`, not only
  modulo `101`.
* `omega_square` — `Ω = c₁ (s₂ − κ t₂²)²` with `κ = −c₂ / (2c₁) ∈ K₅`.
* `c1_ne_zero`, `omega_eq_zero_iff` — `Ω = 0 ↔ s₂ = κ t₂²`.

And modulo `101` (root `w = 9` of `R`): `c₁, c₂, c₃, κ ↦ 69, 8, 50, 38` (`*_at9_mod101`), and
`69 (s − 38 t²)² = 69 s² + 8 t² s + 50 t⁴` in `𝔽₁₀₁` (`omega_mod101_square`).

Not formalized here: that `Ω` is the `E₁` obstruction of the branch-(c) descent (the left null vector and
`RHS_{E₁}` depend on the whole `E₄ → E₃ → E₂` parametrization, whose certificates are not yet in Lean).
Every identity is `linear_combination (cofactor) * hw`; the cofactors are exact quotients by `R` in `ℚ[w]`.
-/

